    "ES measurements were less accurate than ED measurements in relative terms.",
    "Predicted masks systematically underestimated LV area and area-length volumes.",
    "Despite volume underestimation, GT-to-predicted EF bias was close to zero because ED and ES errors can partially cancel in the EF ratio.",
    "Ground-truth-mask geometry itself differed substantially from CAMUS reference EF, demonstrating that downstream EF disagreement cannot be attributed solely to segmentation.",
